  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061x)\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x=1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061x\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
